#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

usage() {
    cat <<'HELP'
Usage: pos-state TARGET STATE ['Note']
       pos-state --help

Set one task's state with Org's own command, and record the change, in
the ClankOS container.
"clankos-run help pos-state" prints the protocol.

    pos-state intray.org:12 DONE 'Sent on Tuesday'
    /path/to/intray.org:12: DONE Send the invoice

TARGET is the task's ID, or FILE:LINE, the file from the working
directory and the line of the task's heading. STATE is TODO, NEXT,
WAITING, SOMEDAY, DONE or CANCELLED. The note is one line.

DONE and CANCELLED add CLOSED. A repeating task set to DONE has its
date moved on by its own repeater and is TODO again, which is how a
review item is marked done. The change is a line in the task's LOGBOOK
drawer, with the note beneath it. Prints the file, the line, and the
state and title the task now has.

Exit: 0 saved, 2 usage, 255 refused or Emacs error, its message on
stderr; 125, 126 and 127 are clankos-run's.
HELP
}

case "${1:-}" in
    ''|help|-h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
esac
exec "$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/clankos-run" pos-state "$@"
